 of USD 10 billion (approximately 14.7 trillion KRW) in investment and infrastructure financing from Nvidia and Brookfield. It has signed an agreement with Nvidia to jointly build an artificial intelligence (AI) factory and for a strategic investment, and intends to work with global alternative investment firm Brookfield to arrange large-scale computing infrastructure, with a plan to expand its AI factory business beyond Asia to Europe·the Middle East.\n\nOn the 27th, Naver disclosed that it will carry out a USD 1 billion (approximately 1.47 trillion KRW) paid-in capital increase allocated to Nvidia, which is pursuing the joint construction of a global AI factory.\n\nThis move is seen as an effort to get ahead in securing business opportunities in the global AI computing market by entering into a strategic partnership with Nvidia in response to surging demand for global AI infrastructure and by jointly building large-scale global AI factories. In the AI factory business, Naver will lead site acquisition, construction, and operation of data centers, while Nvidia will participate as the supplier of graphics processing units (GPUs).\n\nNaver has laid out a phased infrastructure plan to build 55㎿(megawatts) by the first half of 2027, 100㎿ by the end of 2027, and 200㎿ by 2028. Naver also presented a goal of generating revenue from the AI factory business starting in 2027.\n\nThe first hub will be the Naver hyperscaler data center ‘Gak Sejong’, after which it plans to expand across the globe beyond the Asia·Pacific to Europe and the Middle East.\n\nNaver also plans to conduct a USD 1 billion third-party allotment paid-in capital increase, issuing 7,241,564 new common shares to Nvidia at 204,500 KRW per share. It is the first time in 22 years that Naver has undertaken a third-party allotment paid-in capital increase, and the first since its transfer listing to KOSPI in 2008.\n\nIn addition, a plan has been proposed under which Brookfield will arrange USD 9 billion (approximately 13.1625 trillion KRW) in computing infrastructure needed to build the AI factory. Brookfield is a frontier investor in AI infrastructure such as data centers and renewable energy.","fetched":true,"url":"https://www.khan.co.kr/en/article/202607272315027","gurl":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiXkFVX3lxTE14Y1VhTHk0M2NkVDVJRUp0UXVoM0hnNW1Edlc1NVpDcDNqQ2dCSGpWbk1FZnZ0cnY0bVZUX2hGX0RZaTRKZWtVTTY5Nno1XzRjREtzd3c0YWFwTUV6bHc?oc=5","linkOk":true},{"id":"g1hmwajt","cat":"GP","inst":"Apollo","instType":"해외 GP","asset":"PE","region":"GL","date":"07.27","time":"22:17","ts":"2026-07-27T13:17:00.000Z","source":"Investing.com 한국어","lang":"ko","ko":"아폴로, 케펠 해양 에너지 펀드에 15억 달러 투자","en":"","metric":"15억","metricLabel":"핵심 지표","ai":["아폴로, 케펠 해양 에너지 펀드에 15억 달러 투자 Investing.com 한국어"],"body":"아폴로, 케펠 해양 에너지 펀드에 15억 달러 투자 Investing.com 한국어","fetched":false,"url":"https://kr.investing.com/news/company-news/article-93CH-2030369","gurl":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMicEFVX3lxTE5zLUlaTktvcjhFaFpwbTZoY192ZnhLdUdHcGRqOTQ2U0pDLXgyZ25nbjlVdVZpT3dLYlp2TDRqbm90eXFJdGF0Z2ZGZTZkVkZQeWRYMTNKVXhaQTJvNmlFdjVfNDRRVlhnbTF3OEJCa1k?oc=5"},{"id":"g4ntx35","cat":"GP","inst":"Brookfield","instType":"해외 GP","asset":"PE","region":"GL","date":"07.27","time":"22:05","ts":"2026-07-27T13:05:40.000Z","source":"TradingView","lang":"ko","ko":"브룩필드, 사우디아라비아 PIF 등 투자자들로부터 중동 펀드를 위한 20억 달러 조달","en":"","metric":"20억","metricLabel":"핵심 지표","ai":["Federico Maccioni글로벌 투자사 브룩필드 NYSE:BN 는 사우디아라비아의 국부펀드를 비롯한 전략적 앵커 투자자들로부터 약 20억 달러를 조달해, 사우디아라비아 및 중동 전역의 기업에 투자할 사모펀드를 조성했다고 월요일 밝혔다.","이 캐나다 기업은 성명을 통해 ‘브룩필드 미들 이스트 파트너스(BMEP)’ 펀드가 투자 자금의 50%를 사우디아라비아에 배분할 계획이라고 밝혔으며, 해당 펀드가 금융, 산업, 기술 등 다양한 분야의 투자 기회를 모색할 것이라고 덧붙였다.","1조 달러 이상의 자산을 운용 중인 브룩필드는 이 펀드에 5…\n\nLos datos de mercado seleccionados han sido facilitados por ICE Data Services ."],"body":"Federico Maccioni글로벌 투자사 브룩필드 NYSE:BN 는 사우디아라비아의 국부펀드를 비롯한 전략적 앵커 투자자들로부터 약 20억 달러를 조달해, 사우디아라비아 및 중동 전역의 기업에 투자할 사모펀드를 조성했다고 월요일 밝혔다.이 캐나다 기업은 성명을 통해 ‘브룩필드 미들 이스